# Route: guide 43 of 51 of the simulator's completionist route for Tauren
# (1211 of 1222 eligible quests, 160.2 h, world baeac23fbe5e): levels 58 to
# 59, 49 quests, 3.6 h under the model. The order is the simulator's (`sim run
# --objective completionist`, then `sim export`; docs/SIMULATION.md §10): fix
# a step in the exporter or the data, not only here, so the next export keeps
# it.
#
# Flow (The Barrens, Stranglethorn Vale, Badlands, Arathi Highlands, Felwood):
# Ratchet -> The Crossroads -> Camp Taurajo -> The Merchant Coast -> Razorfen
# Kraul -> Camp Taurajo -> The Crossroads -> Lushwater Oasis -> Honor's Stand
# -> Boulder Lode Mine -> Ratchet -> Booty Bay -> Grom'gol Base Camp -> ….
#
# Optional (elite: grouping up is advised): Summoning the Princess (656;
# Myzrael 44); Recover the Key! (7846; Hitah'ya the Keeper 51); Wanted: Vile
# Priestess Hexx and Her Minions (7861; Vile Priestess Hexx 51, Vilebranch
# Aman'zasi Guard 50-51).
#
# Left to other guides: class quests (the Class category); dungeon quests (the
# Dungeons guides): Willix the Importer (1144), Blueleaf Tubers (1221),
# Blueleaf Tubers (1221), Deviate Eradication (1487), Deviate Eradication
# (1487), The Glowing Shard (6981), Find the Gems and Power Source (2339),
# Disharmony of Fire (3907), Commander Gor'shak (3981), The Rise of the
# Machines (4063), KILL ON SIGHT: Dark Iron Dwarves (4081), KILL ON SIGHT:
# High Ranking Dark Iron Officials (4082), Operation: Death to Angerforge
# (4132), Lost Thunderbrew Recipe (4134), Ribbly Screwspigot (4136), The Pack
# Mistress (4724), Kibler's Exotic Pets (4729), The Darkstone Tablet (4768),
# En-Ay-Es-Tee-Why (4862), Warlord's Command (4903), Operative Bijou (4981),
# Dragonmaw Rumors (95663).

